1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,917
(Notice of Permanent Closure)

2
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,229
(Thank you for years of patronage and support.
As of March 17, 2025 we have closed permanently.)

3
00:00:03,253 --> 00:00:07,373
(This is now private property and closed to
the public. Thank you for your cooperation.)

4
00:00:33,116 --> 00:00:34,451
Nakarai-san.

5
00:00:41,757 --> 00:00:43,374
Everything started

6
00:00:43,457 --> 00:00:45,287
with an email sent by mistake.

7
00:00:51,877 --> 00:00:55,794
Did you get an email
with a foodie map today?

8
00:00:55,877 --> 00:00:58,867
I meant to send that to myself,
but it went to you by mistake.

9
00:00:59,417 --> 00:01:02,497
Sorry to bother you. My apologies.

10
00:01:03,677 --> 00:01:06,750
I've been living with my
girlfriend for two years.

11
00:01:07,817 --> 00:01:09,069
However,

12
00:01:09,152 --> 00:01:11,655
there's one thing that's
really bothering me.

13
00:01:12,577 --> 00:01:13,877
And that is...

14
00:01:14,457 --> 00:01:17,817
I live with my best friend from school.

15
00:01:18,557 --> 00:01:20,157
He's a guy, obviously.

16
00:01:20,837 --> 00:01:23,357
And yet, I've fallen for him.

17
00:01:24,257 --> 00:01:25,557
I want to make love to him.

18
00:01:26,077 --> 00:01:27,562
I'm dying for him to hold me.

19
00:01:32,737 --> 00:01:34,037
What are you doing?

20
00:01:37,931 --> 00:01:42,853
I'm dating the girl I love, we live
together, and we'll probably get married.

21
00:01:43,617 --> 00:01:48,277
It really bothers me, though I guess it's
not a big deal in the grand scheme of things.

22
00:01:48,817 --> 00:01:52,537
It's so sweet of you to
keep all this bottled up.

23
00:01:53,177 --> 00:01:56,657
You love her, so you don't
want to make her uncomfortable,

24
00:01:57,217 --> 00:01:59,274
and you don't want to start a fight, right?

25
00:01:59,357 --> 00:02:04,334
The stranger I'd been
pouring my heart out to

26
00:02:04,417 --> 00:02:06,553
turned out to be a coworker
who started at the same time as me.

27
00:02:06,577 --> 00:02:08,097
Maybe the only reason I'm nice to her

28
00:02:09,377 --> 00:02:11,677
is so she'll sleep with me.

29
00:02:13,617 --> 00:02:15,017
It makes me feel like.

30
00:02:15,857 --> 00:02:18,057
I'm just a selfish creep
driven by my own desires.

31
00:02:19,337 --> 00:02:20,914
I'm honestly so sick of myself.

32
00:02:20,997 --> 00:02:22,517
Maybe next time.

33
00:02:24,537 --> 00:02:25,897
It's getting really late.

34
00:02:36,323 --> 00:02:37,716
Are you still up?

35
00:02:38,742 --> 00:02:40,619
I don't really know how to put this,

36
00:02:41,495 --> 00:02:43,054
but please just write me back.

37
00:02:43,955 --> 00:02:44,973
I...

38
00:02:45,582 --> 00:02:47,459
I want to make love with you, Nakarai-san.

39
00:02:49,337 --> 00:02:50,337
Yeah.

40
00:02:52,237 --> 00:02:53,237
Okay.

41
00:02:53,657 --> 00:02:54,841
When it rains, it pours.

42
00:02:55,592 --> 00:02:56,802
Somehow,

43
00:02:56,885 --> 00:02:58,994
that feels just like the two of us.

44
00:02:59,077 --> 00:03:00,931
How could anyone resist this body?

45
00:03:02,077 --> 00:03:04,337
Saying that right now is totally unfair.

46
00:03:06,478 --> 00:03:07,996
You almost made me cry.

47
00:03:10,397 --> 00:03:11,397
Well,

48
00:03:12,177 --> 00:03:13,657
I'm just telling the truth.

49
00:03:17,517 --> 00:03:18,817
Hagiwara,

50
00:03:20,077 --> 00:03:22,334
you're not wrong, and you're not dirty.

51
00:03:22,417 --> 00:03:25,877
What I'd always lacked,
what I'd always craved.

52
00:03:26,790 --> 00:03:28,183
Like praying for rain,

53
00:03:28,834 --> 00:03:30,585
it was what I desperately longed for.

54
00:03:31,128 --> 00:03:32,128
Say it.

55
00:03:32,457 --> 00:03:33,897
I need to hear it from you, Kazuaki.

56
00:03:34,437 --> 00:03:35,507
Just say it.

57
00:03:44,057 --> 00:03:45,692
I've fallen for someone else.

58
00:03:49,312 --> 00:03:50,705
I want to break up.

59
00:03:57,154 --> 00:03:58,171
Goodbye.

60
00:03:59,977 --> 00:04:01,537
Just take it slow.

61
00:04:04,857 --> 00:04:05,857
I'm going to

62
00:04:06,997 --> 00:04:08,297
take my time, too,

63
00:04:10,557 --> 00:04:12,497
and move forward on my own two feet.

64
00:04:13,777 --> 00:04:15,857
What do you mean, you might disappear?

65
00:04:18,977 --> 00:04:20,477
I'm not going anywhere.

66
00:04:21,428 --> 00:04:23,680
Though it is a long story.

67
00:04:26,308 --> 00:04:27,350
Never mind, then.

68
00:04:27,893 --> 00:04:28,893
Liar.

69
00:04:35,837 --> 00:04:37,237
I love you, Hagiwara.

70
00:04:40,617 --> 00:04:42,017
I want to be with you.

71
00:04:46,383 --> 00:04:47,968
I want to be with you, too.

72
00:04:48,205 --> 00:04:49,205
Always

73
00:04:49,581 --> 00:04:50,582
on a rainy day.

74
00:04:51,792 --> 00:04:52,834
Always

75
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:55,061
in the rain.

76
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:45,300
When it rains, it pours:
Mellow Rain (Episode 1)

77
00:05:46,437 --> 00:05:49,057
Well then, welcome back, Hagiwara-san!

78
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:50,183
Thanks.

79
00:05:51,197 --> 00:05:52,497
Cheers!

80
00:05:56,398 --> 00:05:57,398
That hits the spot.

81
00:06:01,157 --> 00:06:02,404
When you were in Osaka,

82
00:06:02,487 --> 00:06:03,922
did you try the herring roe kimchi?

83
00:06:04,990 --> 00:06:06,454
I didn't get a chance to.

84
00:06:06,537 --> 00:06:07,777
Didn't have time to go buy any.

85
00:06:07,897 --> 00:06:10,217
Come on, after I went out of
my way to email you about it?

86
00:06:11,177 --> 00:06:14,557
I saw it on TV and it looked amazing.

87
00:06:16,237 --> 00:06:17,794
I'm so jealous.

88
00:06:17,877 --> 00:06:20,593
Being on a temp assignment instead
of a short business trip is so nice.

89
00:06:20,617 --> 00:06:23,033
You get to actually live in
different places for a little while.

90
00:06:23,057 --> 00:06:24,714
That's what I thought at first, too.

91
00:06:24,797 --> 00:06:29,574
I only went sightseeing in the beginning. By
the end, I just slept through my days off.

92
00:06:29,657 --> 00:06:30,957
Oh, really?

93
00:06:32,457 --> 00:06:33,954
Pardon the interruption.

94
00:06:34,037 --> 00:06:35,877
Here's your salted beef
tongue and short ribs.

95
00:06:38,957 --> 00:06:40,174
Thank you.

96
00:06:40,257 --> 00:06:41,557
Enjoy.

97
00:06:42,497 --> 00:06:43,654
Hold on!

98
00:06:43,737 --> 00:06:46,257
Didn't I tell you that you always
start with the salted tongue?

99
00:06:57,797 --> 00:07:00,037
You haven't changed a bit, Hagiwara.

100
00:07:00,629 --> 00:07:02,897
I was only gone four
months. Why would I change?

101
00:07:10,077 --> 00:07:12,977
By the way, is your place
looking any more livable yet?

102
00:07:13,817 --> 00:07:14,868
Still the same.

103
00:07:15,685 --> 00:07:16,885
What do you mean by "livable"?

104
00:07:17,597 --> 00:07:20,333
Oh right, you haven't been to his
new place yet, have you, Hagiwara-san?

105
00:07:20,357 --> 00:07:20,794
Right.

106
00:07:20,877 --> 00:07:23,652
It's a run-down, forty-year-old
apartment building.

107
00:07:23,735 --> 00:07:24,754
Thirty-seven years.

108
00:07:24,837 --> 00:07:26,534
Same difference.

109
00:07:26,617 --> 00:07:30,284
It's old, so the landlord lets him do pretty
much whatever DIY renovations he wants.

110
00:07:30,367 --> 00:07:33,120
And yet he gave up halfway
through building a shelf.

111
00:07:33,203 --> 00:07:34,403
Why were you building a shelf?

112
00:07:36,697 --> 00:07:38,254
Just felt like it.

113
00:07:38,337 --> 00:07:39,637
Out of nowhere.

114
00:07:42,497 --> 00:07:45,132
Hagiwara-san, could you give him a hand?

115
00:07:45,215 --> 00:07:46,373
You can even charge him for it.

116
00:07:46,397 --> 00:07:47,533
Hey, don't volunteer me for stuff.

117
00:07:47,557 --> 00:07:48,957
We can't leave it like that.

118
00:07:49,977 --> 00:07:52,674
A messy home leads to a messy mind.

119
00:07:52,757 --> 00:07:53,774
Here.

120
00:07:53,857 --> 00:07:54,874
I'm down.

121
00:07:54,957 --> 00:07:56,873
If you don't mind having
me, I'd be happy to help.

122
00:07:56,897 --> 00:07:58,197
Though I'm a total amateur.

123
00:08:02,177 --> 00:08:03,957
See? That works out great!

124
00:08:04,797 --> 00:08:05,594
Dig in.

125
00:08:05,677 --> 00:08:06,677
Thanks.

126
00:08:22,259 --> 00:08:25,652
(From: Nakarai Sei, New Copo Mizunomori 102,
2-8-2 Mizunomori, Arakawa-ku, Tokyo 116-0005)

127
00:08:28,675 --> 00:08:29,884
It's so hot.

128
00:08:41,020 --> 00:08:45,064
(Special Price: Large Watermelon, 700 yen)

129
00:08:54,826 --> 00:08:57,829
He said he wanted to be with me,

130
00:09:02,437 --> 00:09:04,794
but even after we both became single,

131
00:09:04,877 --> 00:09:08,965
it didn't automatically turn
into, "Okay, let's start dating now."

132
00:09:16,617 --> 00:09:17,917
What are you holding?

133
00:09:23,597 --> 00:09:24,622
A watermelon.

134
00:09:26,017 --> 00:09:27,025
Why?

135
00:09:30,197 --> 00:09:31,237
Good question.

136
00:09:33,097 --> 00:09:34,397
What the heck?

137
00:09:50,217 --> 00:09:51,517
Look at this.

138
00:09:55,477 --> 00:09:57,314
Height marks?

139
00:09:57,397 --> 00:09:59,094
Probably.

140
00:09:59,177 --> 00:10:03,437
There are nail holes and peeled-off
sticker marks everywhere, too.

141
00:10:03,997 --> 00:10:06,957
But I loved it the second I saw it
and signed the lease right away.

142
00:10:07,982 --> 00:10:11,027
With no tall buildings
around, the sky looks huge.

143
00:10:13,777 --> 00:10:15,414
What do you want to drink?

144
00:10:15,497 --> 00:10:18,294
I've got barley tea, iced coffee, and beer.

145
00:10:18,377 --> 00:10:19,514
Barley tea.

146
00:10:19,597 --> 00:10:20,597
And?

147
00:10:21,837 --> 00:10:23,597
What comes after "the sky looks huge"?

148
00:10:28,577 --> 00:10:30,297
I also like that it's far from the station.

149
00:10:30,577 --> 00:10:33,157
I wanted a bit of a walk
home, so it's perfect.

150
00:10:35,817 --> 00:10:37,117
I see.

151
00:10:40,057 --> 00:10:41,057
Here.

152
00:10:41,537 --> 00:10:42,559
Thanks.

153
00:10:46,737 --> 00:10:50,177
Anyway, do you really like
watermelon that much, Hagiwara?

154
00:10:50,717 --> 00:10:51,834
Not really.

155
00:10:51,917 --> 00:10:53,654
I haven't had it once this year.

156
00:10:53,737 --> 00:10:55,113
Then you don't even like it!

157
00:10:56,217 --> 00:10:57,054
What are we gonna do with it?

158
00:10:57,137 --> 00:10:58,677
This thing is massive.

159
00:10:59,217 --> 00:11:01,214
It's never gonna fit in my fridge.

160
00:11:01,297 --> 00:11:02,134
My bad.

161
00:11:02,217 --> 00:11:03,457
I'll just take it home with me.

162
00:11:03,537 --> 00:11:04,617
What are you talking about?

163
00:11:05,297 --> 00:11:06,817
It's just taking up space here, right?

164
00:11:07,517 --> 00:11:10,937
If we don't have anything to put
it in, let's just go buy something.

165
00:11:13,317 --> 00:11:14,114
A fridge?

166
00:11:14,197 --> 00:11:15,497
As if.

167
00:11:23,297 --> 00:11:24,597
This is great.

168
00:11:25,117 --> 00:11:27,573
Looks like the kind of tub that drops
on people's heads in comedy skits.

169
00:11:27,597 --> 00:11:28,597
It's got a classic vibe.

170
00:11:29,439 --> 00:11:30,523
What kind of vibe?

171
00:11:31,357 --> 00:11:33,753
What else are you ever gonna use
this for besides chilling a watermelon?

172
00:11:33,777 --> 00:11:34,534
Plenty of things.

173
00:11:34,617 --> 00:11:36,154
Like what?

174
00:11:36,237 --> 00:11:40,797
If my water heater ever dies on me, I
can use it to wash up on the balcony.

175
00:11:41,357 --> 00:11:44,354
And if my washing machine
breaks, I can wash my clothes in it.

176
00:11:44,437 --> 00:11:45,774
That's a huge stretch.

177
00:11:45,857 --> 00:11:46,873
Who cares?

178
00:11:49,667 --> 00:11:52,086
We need it right now,
and that's all that matters.

179
00:11:53,087 --> 00:11:55,481
Doesn't matter what happens to it tomorrow.

180
00:11:56,637 --> 00:11:58,117
That's pretty bold of you.

181
00:11:58,617 --> 00:11:59,617
You think?

182
00:12:04,057 --> 00:12:05,225
Is it raining?

183
00:12:06,177 --> 00:12:07,811
Let's make a run for it.

184
00:12:07,894 --> 00:12:09,787
Look, it's coming in handy already!

185
00:12:10,677 --> 00:12:11,977
Whoa!

186
00:12:18,317 --> 00:12:19,823
It's so loud!

187
00:12:19,906 --> 00:12:21,241
This is crazy!

188
00:12:21,324 --> 00:12:22,617
I can't hear a thing!

189
00:12:27,163 --> 00:12:28,163
Here, I'll hold it.

190
00:12:50,097 --> 00:12:51,104
I love you.

191
00:12:54,417 --> 00:12:55,500
I can't hear you!

192
00:12:56,779 --> 00:12:57,916
Huh?

193
00:12:57,999 --> 00:12:59,594
Oh...

194
00:12:59,677 --> 00:13:00,977
I said...

195
00:13:04,937 --> 00:13:06,257
You totally heard me, didn't you?

196
00:13:06,877 --> 00:13:08,397
I told you, I couldn't hear anything.

197
00:13:09,897 --> 00:13:11,697
I just read your lips.

198
00:13:13,293 --> 00:13:14,310
Seriously...

199
00:13:18,377 --> 00:13:20,597
So much for "not going anywhere."

200
00:13:22,877 --> 00:13:23,877
I'm sorry.

201
00:13:25,757 --> 00:13:28,277
I thought you were already over it.

202
00:13:29,597 --> 00:13:30,897
Huh?

203
00:13:31,617 --> 00:13:33,817
I figured after having
some time to cool off,

204
00:13:34,637 --> 00:13:38,137
maybe you didn't care about me anymore.

205
00:13:40,097 --> 00:13:41,397
Not a chance.

206
00:14:11,677 --> 00:14:15,237
Do you have any idea how many times I got off
thinking about you after that, Nakarai-san?

207
00:14:15,813 --> 00:14:17,315
How on earth would I know that?

208
00:14:18,277 --> 00:14:21,697
I lost count, too. Point is, a lot.

209
00:14:22,653 --> 00:14:23,988
Come on...

210
00:14:34,997 --> 00:14:39,117
I remember everything we did that night, but
what really stuck with me was the next morning.

211
00:14:39,504 --> 00:14:40,922
The way you smiled at me.

212
00:14:42,657 --> 00:14:43,657
Did I?

213
00:14:44,877 --> 00:14:48,457
You looked so gorgeous and adorable.

214
00:14:49,297 --> 00:14:50,640
It made me feel...

215
00:14:50,723 --> 00:14:52,533
purely happy.

216
00:14:56,017 --> 00:14:57,263
Stop it.

217
00:14:58,117 --> 00:14:59,117
Why?

218
00:14:59,657 --> 00:15:03,437
You're setting the bar way too high now.

219
00:15:09,277 --> 00:15:13,321
What kind of face am I supposed
to make after we're done later?

220
00:15:20,377 --> 00:15:22,817
Then don't think about after.

221
00:15:23,457 --> 00:15:24,977
We're just getting started, aren't we?

222
00:15:44,944 --> 00:15:46,003
Nakarai-san.

223
00:15:46,997 --> 00:15:48,030
What?

224
00:15:49,537 --> 00:15:52,537
I want your answer to what I said earlier.

225
00:15:55,830 --> 00:15:57,123
Right now?

226
00:15:58,332 --> 00:16:00,242
Harder for you to say
no right now, isn't it?

227
00:16:09,051 --> 00:16:10,344
I like you.

228
00:16:26,194 --> 00:16:27,244
Hagiwara.

229
00:16:28,613 --> 00:16:29,613
Hmm?

230
00:16:33,868 --> 00:16:35,077
Even if you get tired of me,

231
00:16:36,746 --> 00:16:38,681
don't get tired of my body.

232
00:16:40,541 --> 00:16:42,341
Isn't it supposed to be
the other way around?

233
00:16:43,037 --> 00:16:44,086
Right.

234
00:16:46,097 --> 00:16:47,497
That's supposed to be my line.

235
00:16:52,299 --> 00:16:53,599
Yeah.

236
00:17:03,297 --> 00:17:04,817
It's not very cold.

237
00:17:06,016 --> 00:17:07,697
I figured as much.

238
00:17:09,570 --> 00:17:10,963
The seeds are such a pain.

239
00:17:13,977 --> 00:17:17,111
Come to think of it, I never
did finish building those shelves.

240
00:17:18,457 --> 00:17:19,837
You finally noticed.

241
00:17:21,337 --> 00:17:22,637
I'm starving, though.

242
00:17:24,085 --> 00:17:25,086
True.

243
00:17:25,597 --> 00:17:27,336
Watermelon alone isn't gonna fill us up.

244
00:17:30,877 --> 00:17:32,177
What are you in the mood for?

245
00:17:40,797 --> 00:17:41,974
I've got it!

246
00:17:42,057 --> 00:17:43,154
What?

247
00:17:43,237 --> 00:17:44,754
Hand-rolled sushi.

248
00:17:44,837 --> 00:17:46,734
I want hand-rolled sushi.

249
00:17:46,817 --> 00:17:48,193
At a sushi place?

250
00:17:48,276 --> 00:17:49,734
No, at home.

251
00:17:49,817 --> 00:17:51,880
We'll hit the supermarket,
grab whatever fillings we want,

252
00:17:51,904 --> 00:17:54,323
load up a wooden tub with
rice, and roll as many as we want.

253
00:17:55,116 --> 00:17:56,554
Do you even have a wooden tub?

254
00:17:56,637 --> 00:17:57,637
Nope.

255
00:17:58,257 --> 00:17:59,996
I don't, so we're going to buy one.

256
00:18:00,079 --> 00:18:01,372
At the shopping arcade.

257
00:18:01,917 --> 00:18:03,217
We're going back there again?

258
00:18:22,727 --> 00:18:24,604
Hey, Hagiwara.

259
00:18:24,687 --> 00:18:25,687
What?

260
00:18:26,497 --> 00:18:28,858
Something good happened to you, didn't it?

261
00:18:28,941 --> 00:18:29,794
Huh?

262
00:18:29,877 --> 00:18:30,914
Not at all.

263
00:18:30,997 --> 00:18:32,274
No, you're lying.

264
00:18:32,357 --> 00:18:34,177
You're practically glowing.

265
00:18:35,239 --> 00:18:36,324
That's creepy.

266
00:18:40,537 --> 00:18:42,217
Even if something did, my lips are sealed.

267
00:18:44,277 --> 00:18:45,577
Fine, whatever.

268
00:18:53,397 --> 00:18:55,134
I'm heading out.

269
00:18:55,217 --> 00:18:56,134
See ya.

270
00:18:56,217 --> 00:18:57,517
Good work today.

271
00:19:44,100 --> 00:19:45,393
We had a deal, didn't we?

272
00:19:47,353 --> 00:19:49,121
Not to ruin anything.

273
00:19:51,777 --> 00:19:52,942
We did.

274
00:19:54,277 --> 00:19:55,361
I know.

275
00:20:00,977 --> 00:20:02,277
But...

276
00:20:03,757 --> 00:20:05,797
the second I saw your
face, I couldn't help myself.

277
00:20:27,417 --> 00:20:29,574
Did you get locked in again?

278
00:20:29,657 --> 00:20:30,957
Heck no.

279
00:20:35,517 --> 00:20:36,814
Yesterday,

280
00:20:36,897 --> 00:20:38,377
I used that wooden tub again.

281
00:20:39,317 --> 00:20:40,954
Hand-rolled sushi by yourself?

282
00:20:41,037 --> 00:20:43,197
No, chirashi sushi.

283
00:20:44,037 --> 00:20:47,937
I bought a seasoning mix and
topped it with egg and frozen edamame.

284
00:20:48,497 --> 00:20:50,174
Sounds delicious.

285
00:20:50,257 --> 00:20:55,357
I made way too much, though. Had it for
lunch today, and probably dinner tonight.

286
00:20:58,917 --> 00:21:00,050
What about the watermelon?

287
00:21:00,937 --> 00:21:01,944
Still working on it.

288
00:21:02,557 --> 00:21:03,834
How about yours?

289
00:21:03,917 --> 00:21:04,917
Same here.

290
00:21:04,977 --> 00:21:08,374
Every time I open the fridge,
I'm like, "Oh, you're still here."

291
00:21:08,457 --> 00:21:10,137
It catches me off guard every single time.

292
00:21:10,561 --> 00:21:12,288
Remind me whose idea it was to buy it?

293
00:21:27,057 --> 00:21:29,877
It's been a while since we met up here.

294
00:21:31,777 --> 00:21:33,354
After what happened,

295
00:21:33,437 --> 00:21:36,837
even the security guard was speechless,
and I'm in General Affairs, no less.

296
00:21:37,657 --> 00:21:39,097
Well, can you blame him?

297
00:21:48,357 --> 00:21:49,757
I'm heading home.

298
00:21:50,777 --> 00:21:52,353
You should head back soon, too...

299
00:22:02,297 --> 00:22:03,564
I want a do-over.

300
00:22:05,282 --> 00:22:06,282
Huh?

301
00:22:07,368 --> 00:22:08,368
Last time...

302
00:22:09,317 --> 00:22:11,037
when we parted ways here,

303
00:22:12,257 --> 00:22:13,957
it really hurt.

304
00:22:14,897 --> 00:22:16,397
And it ate me up inside.

305
00:22:18,837 --> 00:22:20,877
I want to overwrite it with a good memory.

306
00:22:30,403 --> 00:22:31,703
Don't laugh.

307
00:22:33,102 --> 00:22:34,495
I'm not laughing.

308
00:22:36,647 --> 00:22:38,040
You totally are.

309
00:22:40,484 --> 00:22:41,777
Who knows?

310
00:22:54,790 --> 00:22:56,183
Let's overwrite that memory, then.

311
00:22:59,253 --> 00:23:00,253
Yeah.

312
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:15,760
(Next Episode Preview)

313
00:23:15,843 --> 00:23:16,754
Whoa.

314
00:23:16,837 --> 00:23:18,354
Don't "whoa" me.

315
00:23:18,437 --> 00:23:20,094
I'm the one doing all the work anyway.

316
00:23:20,177 --> 00:23:22,693
By the way, heard you
broke up with your girlfriend?

317
00:23:22,776 --> 00:23:25,314
Let me set you up with someone new.

318
00:23:25,397 --> 00:23:27,034
Your friend is really handsome, too.

319
00:23:27,117 --> 00:23:28,474
Do you have a girlfriend?

320
00:23:28,557 --> 00:23:29,974
Seeing anyone?

321
00:23:30,057 --> 00:23:31,214
Of course I am.

322
00:23:31,297 --> 00:23:32,494
Today,

323
00:23:32,577 --> 00:23:34,114
you're treating me.

324
00:23:34,197 --> 00:23:35,874
A donation for the festival.

325
00:23:35,957 --> 00:23:37,353
Sorry, I have no idea
what you're talking about.

326
00:23:37,377 --> 00:23:38,677
Come to think of it,

327
00:23:39,697 --> 00:23:40,774
why a queen-size?

328
00:23:40,857 --> 00:23:41,574
Why a what?

329
00:23:41,657 --> 00:23:43,114
The bed.

330
00:23:43,197 --> 00:23:43,914
Is that a problem?

331
00:23:43,997 --> 00:23:46,914
It's not a problem, per se,
but didn't you notice anything?

332
00:23:46,997 --> 00:23:47,997
Wait a second.

333
00:23:48,057 --> 00:23:49,177
How did it end up like this?

334
00:23:49,257 --> 00:23:51,594
Why are we even mad at each other?

335
00:23:51,677 --> 00:23:53,054
Hold still.

336
00:23:53,137 --> 00:23:55,234
The honey smell is so strong.

337
00:23:55,317 --> 00:23:57,037
It's gonna attract ants.

338
00:23:57,577 --> 00:23:59,697
I'll pounce on you before
the ants even get a chance.
